    {
      "id": "48ec6545-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Articulation Agreement Overview This agreement outlines lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Students are strongly encouraged to consult an academic advisor to ensure they meet all degree requirements for their intended baccalaureate program. Helpful Resources: CSUB Catalog Transfer Admission Requirements Academic Advising Student Centers CSUB Program Pathways Mapper Course Equivalency Information for 4-Year Institutions Students and staff can explore course transfer equivalencies through the Transfer Evaluation System (TES) . Equivalency agreements are updated regularly and subject to change. For the most current information, please refer to TES or contact the Articulation Office .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>Articulation Agreement Overview</strong></p><p>This agreement outlines lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Students are strongly encouraged to consult an academic advisor to ensure they meet all degree requirements for their intended baccalaureate program.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Helpful Resources:</strong></p><ul><li><a href=\"https://catalog.csub.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUB Catalog</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/admissions/transfer\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Admission Requirements</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/advising\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Advising Student Centers</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/ppm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUB Program Pathways Mapper</a></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Course Equivalency Information for 4-Year Institutions</strong></p><p>Students and staff can explore course transfer equivalencies through the <a href=\"https://tes.collegesource.com/publicview/TES_publicview01.aspx?rid=7ea49506-39bf-4815-8199-734369e7a30c&amp;aid=ccc830a2-2435-4dd6-b352-a586b4575654\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Evaluation System (TES)</a>. Equivalency agreements are updated regularly and subject to change. For the most current information, please refer to TES or contact the <a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/articulation/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Articulation Office</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "3efe6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About the Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a5367445-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The study of Communications is the essential foundation of all other disciplines because messages are the foundation of the expression of meaning. Communication is at the heart of what it means to be human. The primary purpose of the Communications Program is to prepare students to be sophisticated in their knowledge of the organization and use of the media, as they prepare for careers as communications professionals. The curriculum stresses knowledge of communications processes, an expected proficiency in writing and practice, awareness of professional responsibilities, knowledge of ethical practices, and acquaintance with the laws that govern the use of the mass media. Further, the curriculum addresses the relationships between media and the societies they seek to serve viewed from regional, national, and international perspectives. At CSUB, students in Communications have numerous opportunities for hands-on learning. Journalism students produce both print and online versions of The Runner newspaper, including podcasts and blog entries. Digital Media students create their own video, audio, and interactive media productions. Public Relations students learn how to formulate, develop, and apply communication strategies that present an organization in the best light. The department also offers a minor in Communications : Journalism, Public Relations, and Digital Media. For additional information, visit the following: Department of Communications Program Requirements - Communications, BA, Digital Media Concentration",
      "contentHtml": "<p>The study of Communications is the essential foundation of all other disciplines because messages are the foundation of the expression of meaning. Communication is at the heart of what it means to be human.</p><p><br></p><p>The primary purpose of the Communications Program is to prepare students to be sophisticated in their knowledge of the organization and use of the media, as they prepare for careers as communications professionals. The curriculum stresses knowledge of communications processes, an expected proficiency in writing and practice, awareness of professional responsibilities, knowledge of ethical practices, and acquaintance with the laws that govern the use of the mass media. Further, the curriculum addresses the relationships between media and the societies they seek to serve viewed from regional, national, and international perspectives.</p><p><br></p><p>At CSUB, students in Communications have numerous opportunities for hands-on learning. Journalism students produce both print and online versions of <a href=\"http://therunneronline.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">The Runner</a> newspaper, including podcasts and blog entries. Digital Media students create their own video, audio, and interactive media productions. Public Relations students learn how to formulate, develop, and apply communication strategies that present an organization in the best light.</p><p><br></p><p>The department also offers a <a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/comm/minor-communications\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">minor in Communications</a>: Journalism, Public Relations, and Digital Media.</p><p><br></p><p>For additional information, visit the following:</p><p>Department of <a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/comm/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Communications</a></p><p>Program Requirements - <a href=\"https://catalog.csub.edu/academic-degrees-programs/undergraduate-majors/communications-ba-digital-media-concentration/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Communications, BA, Digital Media Concentration</a></p>"
    },
